 "circuits": [],
 "equations": [],
 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Construction",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Each part is one Schottky barrier junction with a guard ring for protection against overvoltage. Losses are low and efficiency high."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Polarity",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "A line at one end of the body marks the cathode. The marking codes run K12 to K120, one per part number."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Package and soldering",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "SOD-123FL, a low-profile body with flat leads, suited to automatic placement. The moulding compound is rated UL 94V-0, RoHS compliant and halogen-free. The leads are solder plated and solderable to MIL-STD-750 Method 2026. Moisture sensitivity is level 1 to J-STD-020, with a lead-free reflow peak of 260 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Uses",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "High-speed switching, circuit protection and voltage clamping."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Derating",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The full 1.0 A average current holds up to a lead temperature of about 75 °C for DSK12 to DSK16 and about 97 °C for DSK18 to DSK120, then falls in a straight line to 0.2 A at 125 °C and 150 °C respectively (Fig.1). Surge capability drops from about 30 A for one 8.3 ms half-sine cycle to under 6 A over 100 cycles (Fig.2)."
  }
 ],
